<tr id="S5.T1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding:1pt 2.0pt;">GPT3.5 Turbo</th>
<td id="S5.T1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding:1pt 2.0pt;">631</td>
<td id="S5.T1.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding:1pt 2.0pt;">600</td>
<td id="S5.T1.2.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding:1pt 2.0pt;">2</td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T1.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T1.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding:1pt 2.0pt;">DeepSeek</th>
<td id="S5.T1.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding:1pt 2.0pt;">631</td>
<td id="S5.T1.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding:1pt 2.0pt;">600</td>
<td id="S5.T1.2.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding:1pt 2.0pt;">4</td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T1.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T1.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_b ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding:1pt 2.0pt;">DeepSeek</th>
<td id="S5.T1.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding:1pt 2.0pt;">50</td>
<td id="S5.T1.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding:1pt 2.0pt;">50</td>
<td id="S5.T1.2.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding:1pt 2.0pt;">16</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>TreePrompt Hyperparameters and Number of K-NN Executions for Each LLM</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We can obtain the complete prompt sent to the LLM using the following formula:</p>
<table id="S5.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\mathrm{TreePrompt}}=n_{\mathrm{nbr}}\times k_{\mathrm{NN}}+R" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>TreePrompt</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>nbr</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>NN</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\mathrm{TreePrompt}}=n_{\mathrm{nbr}}\times k_{\mathrm{NN}}+R</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S5.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle n_{\mathrm{nbr}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>nbr</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle n_{\mathrm{nbr}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:\text{Number of neighbors in K-NN}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mtext>Number of neighbors in K-NN</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:\text{Number of neighbors in K-NN}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle k_{\mathrm{NN}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>NN</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle k_{\mathrm{NN}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:\text{Number of K-NN executions}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mtext>Number of K-NN executions</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:\text{Number of K-NN executions}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:\text{Number of random examples}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mtext>Number of random examples</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:\text{Number of random examples}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Based on this formula, we calculate the number of prompts generated for each LLM, as detailed in Table 3.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in Table <a href="#S5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 5.2 Analysis of TreePrompt Method ‣ 5 Results ‣ TreePrompt: Leveraging Hierarchical Few-Shot Example Selection for Improved English-Persian and English-German Translation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, the performance of the TreePrompt method is highly sensitive to its parameter settings. Proper tuning of these parameters can significantly reduce computational costs. Specifically, decreasing the number of neighbors leads to more frequent K-NN executions but results in fewer total prompts. In contrast, increasing the number of neighbors and random examples reduces the frequency of K-NN runs while substantially increasing the number of prompts generated. Therefore, a balance must be struck between these parameters to optimize both performance and computational efficiency.</p>
</div>
